---
---

<section class="border-b border-[#222630] bg-[#0a0b0e] py-20 lg:py-24" id="architecture">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-4xl">
        Execution Architecture
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base sm:text-lg text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
        Reptar separates application domain logic from host transport. Your C# compiles either to a cached WebAssembly reactor inside Cloudflare Workers or directly to a standalone Native AOT executable on Kestrel or AWS Lambda.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Clean 4-column structural grid without eyebrow badges -->
    <div class="mt-10 border border-[#222630] bg-[#0f1116]">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-4 divide-y md:divide-y-0 md:divide-x divide-[#222630]">
        <div class="p-6 flex flex-col justify-between">
          <div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between pb-3 border-b border-[#1b1f28]">
              <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">1. Typed Client</h3>
              <span class="font-mono text-xs text-zinc-500">@reptar/client</span>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
              Zero-dependency TypeScript RPC proxy (~100 lines). Infers path parameters, query strings, request payloads, and status-discriminated responses directly from C#.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-6 pt-3 border-t border-[#1b1f28] font-mono text-[11px] text-zinc-400">
            TanStack Start · React 19 · Next.js · Expo
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="p-6 flex flex-col justify-between">
          <div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between pb-3 border-b border-[#1b1f28]">
              <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">2. Host Transport</h3>
              <span class="font-mono text-xs text-zinc-500">workerd / Kestrel</span>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
              On Cloudflare Workers, the thin TS host shim bridges WebCrypto, cookies, and bindings. On Linux/Docker, <code class="text-zinc-200 font-mono">Reptar.Kestrel</code> pumps raw <code class="text-zinc-200 font-mono">PipeReader</code> spans with zero intermediate stream copies.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-6 pt-3 border-t border-[#1b1f28] font-mono text-[11px] text-zinc-400">
            PipeReader / PipeWriter · JSImport Bridge
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="p-6 flex flex-col justify-between bg-[#13161c]">
          <div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between pb-3 border-b border-[#222630]">
              <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">3. Reptar C# Core</h3>
              <span class="font-mono text-xs text-emerald-400">Wasm / Native AOT</span>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
              Zero-allocation radix router, <code class="text-zinc-100 font-mono">CacheControl.SWR</code> perimeter cache, O(1) sliding-window rate limiter, <code class="text-zinc-100 font-mono">Rule&lt;T&gt;</code> validation, and <code class="text-zinc-100 font-mono">SourceGenJsonCodec</code> UTF-8 serialization.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-6 pt-3 border-t border-[#222630] font-mono text-[11px] text-emerald-400">
            0 Reflection · 10.9 MB AOT Binary
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="p-6 flex flex-col justify-between">
          <div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between pb-3 border-b border-[#1b1f28]">
              <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">4. Data &amp; Edge Bindings</h3>
              <span class="font-mono text-xs text-zinc-500">c.Db / c.Storage</span>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
              Compile-time <code class="text-zinc-200 font-mono">[ReptarEntity]</code> mappers read directly from <code class="text-zinc-200 font-mono">DbDataReader</code> ordinals. Supports 32-channel WAL read pools on SQLite, pipelined <code class="text-zinc-200 font-mono">NpgsqlBatch</code> on Postgres, MySQL, and Cloudflare D1/R2/KV/AI.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-6 pt-3 border-t border-[#1b1f28] font-mono text-[11px] text-zinc-400">
            D1 · SQLite WAL · PostgreSQL · MySQL
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Lifecycle Detail Row -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 border-t border-[#222630] divide-y md:divide-y-0 md:divide-x divide-[#222630] bg-[#0c0e12]">
        <div class="p-5">
          <div class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-white">Isolate &amp; Process Reuse</div>
          <p class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
            In Cloudflare Workers, the Wasm module is instantiated once per isolate and reused across requests (&lt;2 ms warm execution). In Native AOT containers, the binary boots in 258 ms with zero JIT warmup.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-5">
          <div class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-white">Positional Entity Mapping</div>
          <p class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
            When SQL columns match your <code class="text-zinc-200 font-mono">[ReptarEntity]</code> constructor order, Reptar invokes a static <code class="text-zinc-200 font-mono">MapPositional</code> delegate using constant column indices (<code class="text-zinc-200 font-mono">0, 1, 2...</code>) with zero string lookups or closures.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-5">
          <div class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-white">Pipelined Write Batching</div>
          <p class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
            Multi-statement writes execute via <code class="text-zinc-200 font-mono">c.Db.BatchAsync(...)</code>—using a single <code class="text-zinc-200 font-mono">NpgsqlBatch</code> network round-trip on PostgreSQL, atomic batching on Cloudflare D1, and pre-gate command building on SQLite.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
